==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
                                                                                             Midnight Animation Format Specification
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Brief: Binary Format used to store animation data. 
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
                                                                                                            File Layout
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================

int  { 4Bytes }               Date Length
char { 1Byte * Date Length }  Actual Date

int  { 4Bytes }               Name Length
char { 1Byte * Name Length }  Actual Name

int  { 4Bytes }               Type Length
char { 1Byte * Type Length }  Actual type

int  { 4Bytes }               Name Length
char { 1Byte * Name Length }  Actual Name

int  { 4Bytes }               Frame Count --- Number of frames that the animation has
int  { 4Bytes }               Frame Rate  --- Animation framerate
int  { 4Bytes }               Joint Count --- Number of joint transformations per frame

Frames[ Frame Count ]
{	
    #------------------------------------------[40 Bytes]-----------------------------------------#         | Each joint transformation is 40 bytes
	#--------------------------# #-----------------------------------# #--------------------------#         | and each frame contains 'joint count' transformations 
	| PositX | PositY | PositZ | | OrienX | OrienY | OrienZ | OrienW | | ScaleX | ScaleY | ScaleZ |         |
	|--------|--------|--------| |--------|--------|--------|--------| |--------|--------|--------|         |
	| 4Bytes | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | | 4bytes | 4bytes | 4bytes |         |
	| 4Bytes | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | | 4bytes | 4bytes | 4bytes |         |
	| 4Bytes | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | 4Bytes | | 4bytes | 4bytes | 4bytes |         |
	# ...... | ...... | ...... # # ...... | ...... | ...... | ...... # # ...... | ...... | ...... |         |
}

==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
																											    Legend
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================

 - PositX: Joint position X 
 - PositY: Joint position Y 
 - PositZ: Joint position Z 
 
 - OrienX: Joint orientation X 
 - OrienY: Joint orientation Y 
 - OrienZ: Joint orientation Z 
 - OrienW: Joint orientation real value W
 
 - ScaleX: Joint scale X
 - ScaleY: Joint scale Y
 - ScaleZ: Joint scale Z
 
 
 ==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
																											    NOTES
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================

- The animation type can be Raw or Hierarchical. 
- Raw animations export the final joint transformations with all of their constraints and parent relationships applied to them. So in Midnight the joint Animated transform would be equal to the currentFrame transform.
		No need to calculate the relationships at runtime, they are exported already precalculated.
- Hierarchical animations data just exports the decomposed joint matrix. It needs to be calculated at runtime.

- Right now only Raw animations are working.

- For the skeleton representation of the mesh. I need to combine the skeleton's default joint position which are inside the MOF file and multiply them with the currentFrame transformation


- Even tough in Blender you can modify a bone and the transformations seem to apply relative to that bone visual transformation in space, all of the resulting transformations data start with <0, 0, 0> as their default position <0,0,0,1> for the orientation and <1, 1, 1>  for the scaling. 
		Example: If the pose bone hasn't changed from the  edit bone position, the resulting transformation position will be <0, 0, 0> otherwise the mesh would appear <nX, nY, nZ> units apart from the bone. 
		So for example if a vertex with it's origin in <0, 0, 0> had an offset of -1 in x and a bone at the same position <-1, 0, 0> is transforming said vertex, the resulting transformations should initiate from <0, 0, 0> if otherwise starts from the 
		bone's position <-1, 0, 0> the vertex final position will be wrong by it's position (relative to the mesh pivot point) <-1, 0, 0> + the bone position (relative to the armature's pivot point) <-1, 0, 0> resulting to <-2, 0, 0> as it's default transformation. 
		That's why even tough visually you are modifying the vertex using the offseted bone, the resulting transformation starts from the armature pivot which is set to <0,0,0> as it's default position <0,0,0,1> as it's default orientation and <1,1,1> as it's default scale when exporting the MOF file